#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:5
msgid "The per-namespace NFS client keyring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:7
msgid ""
"The NFS client holds one keyring, named \".nfs\", per network namespace. An "
"xprtsec=mtls mount presents the client certificate and private key named by "
"its cert_serial= and privkey_serial= mount options, and the handshake links "
"the mount's namespace .nfs keyring into tlshd before tlshd reads those keys. "
"Keys placed on the .nfs keyring therefore need not grant user read "
"permission: tlshd reaches them as a possessor, and a tlshd in another "
"network namespace never possesses them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:16
msgid ""
"The keyring is owned by the owner of the network namespace's user namespace, "
"with KEY_POS_ALL and KEY_USR_ALL less SETATTR. It is not charged to any "
"quota. Keys added to it by userspace are charged to the user that adds them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:22
msgid "Finding the keyring serial number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:24
msgid ""
"The .nfs keyring is not linked into any keyring that userspace possesses, so "
"a serial number is the only way to name it. The NFS client registers a key "
"type, \"nfs_keyring\", whose sole purpose is to hand that serial number out. "
"Its request_key handler runs in the caller's context and does not upcall to /"
"sbin/request-key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:30
msgid ""
"To obtain the serial number, request a key of type \"nfs_keyring\" with the "
"description \".nfs\" and read its payload::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:36
msgid "The contract of the key type is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:38
msgid ""
"The description is the string \".nfs\". Any other description is rejected "
"with EINVAL before a key is allocated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:41
msgid ""
"The callout info must be present. request_key() with a NULL callout_info "
"never invokes a handler and returns ENOKEY when no matching key exists, so "
"use request_key() with an empty string, or ``keyctl request2`` rather than "
"``keyctl request``. The content of the callout info is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:47
msgid ""
"The payload is the keyring serial number as decimal ASCII digits with no "
"terminating NUL. The return value of keyctl_read() gives the length; a "
"buffer of 12 bytes is sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:51
msgid ""
"add_key() with this type accepts only that payload. A key carrying any other "
"value is rejected with EINVAL, so a key found in the caller's keyrings "
"always holds the serial number of the caller's namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:56
msgid ""
"The key type carries KEY_TYPE_NET_DOMAIN. A key instantiated in one network "
"namespace does not answer a request made in another, so a process that keeps "
"its session keyring across setns() receives the serial number of the "
"namespace it is in at the time of the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:61
msgid ""
"The serial number is not a secret. The keyring's own permissions decide what "
"a caller can do with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:65
msgid "Provisioning credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../filesystems/nfs/keyring.rst:67
msgid ""
"Add the client certificate and private key to the .nfs keyring as keys that "
"grant no user read permission, then pass their serial numbers as "
"cert_serial= and privkey_serial= mount options."
msgstr ""
